From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikael Hug <mikaelhug@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: Keep Apple silicon root ports in D0

A USB keyboard behind a PCIe xHCI (the USB-A ports of the M2 Mac mini)
does not wake the system from s2idle. The key press does reach the root
port: after such a cycle, ending with the power button, Root Status of
the port holds PME Status with the Requester ID of the xHCI. The PME
interrupt of the port, an MSI, has never fired.

On arm64, pci_bridge_d3_possible() allows every PCIe port into D3, so
the core moves the root port to D3hot once the xHCI below it is in
D3hot. A function in D3hot cannot signal an MSI, and these systems have
no platform wake path such as an ACPI GPE: the MSI of the root port is
the only way a PME can reach the CPUs.

Keep the root ports in D0, so that any PCIe device can wake the system.

---
 drivers/pci/quirks.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/quirks.c b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
--- a/drivers/pci/quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
@@ -2585,6 +2585,20 @@ static void quirk_no_aer_anfe(struct pci_dev *dev)
 }
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_APPLE, 0x1802, quirk_no_aer_anfe);
 
+/*
+ * Apple silicon root ports report a PME from below them only with their own
+ * MSI, which they cannot send from D3hot, and there is no platform wake path.
+ * Keep them in D0 so that PCIe devices can wake the system.
+ */
+static void quirk_apple_root_port_no_d3(struct pci_dev *dev)
+{
+	if (pci_is_pcie(dev) && pci_pcie_type(dev) == PCI_EXP_TYPE_ROOT_PORT)
+		dev->dev_flags |= PCI_DEV_FLAGS_NO_D3;
+}
+DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_CLASS_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_APPLE, PCI_ANY_ID,
+			      PCI_CLASS_BRIDGE_PCI, 8,
+			      quirk_apple_root_port_no_d3);
+
 /*
  * Under some circumstances, AER is not linked with extended capabilities.
  * Force it to be linked by setting the corresponding control bit in the
-- 
